    "result_text": "All 267 tests pass. \n\nThe change is complete. When an owner is created without a registration date, it now defaults to today, and the value is returned as `registrationDate` in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nWhat I changed:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `LocalDate registrationDate` field (Jackson serializes it as `YYYY-MM-DD`).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `registration_date` `LocalDate` column with getter/setter.\n- **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after mapping the request, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when absent. MapStruct maps the field by name in both directions automatically, so no mapper change was needed.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,mysql}/data.sql`** \u2014 made the seed `INSERT INTO owners` statements use an explicit column list so the added column doesn't break positional inserts (h2/postgres already used explicit lists).",
